  "summary": "In 2 Samuel 5:7–9, David captures the stronghold of Zion, which the narrative identifies with the city of David. This places Zion in Jerusalem's royal story. Later passages in the record focus on the temple and its meaning; they connect worship with Jerusalem but do not provide a map of every biblical use of the name Zion.",
  "historical_context": "The relevant narrative in 2 Samuel 5:1–10 describes David taking Jerusalem and its stronghold, Zion, then calling it the city of David. The passage links the names within that account; it does not by itself establish the later boundaries or every use of Zion as a place-name. The other anchors concern temple passages and should not be used to supply an archaeological reconstruction.",
