  "literary_context": "In 2 Samuel 5:7–9, the narrative moves from the capture of Zion to David's residence and building activity in the city. The wording joins the stronghold, Zion, and the city of David in this episode. In 1 Kings 8 and John 2, the focus is instead the temple and its role; keeping these scenes distinct helps readers see the biblical connections without assuming that every reference names the same feature.",
  "covenantal_significance": "These anchors connect Jerusalem's royal and worship traditions through separate scenes. Second Samuel 5 associates Zion with David's kingship; 1 Kings 8 narrates the temple dedication, and John 2 later uses temple language in a dispute about Jesus' authority. The passages invite readers to notice how kingship and worship gather around Jerusalem, while each text makes its own claim and purpose.",
